cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pubmed-stream in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pubmed-stream: From PubMed Searches to Knowledge Graphs of the Biomedical Literature"
authors:
  - name: "Haran Lab, University of Massachusetts"
  - name: "Bucci Lab, University of Massachusetts"
  - name: "Microbiology & Microbiome Dynamics AI HUB, University of Massachusetts"
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/melhzy/pubmed-stream"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/pubmed-stream/"
abstract: >-
  pubmed-stream downloads full-text articles from PubMed Central, maps the
  evidence around key papers through PubMed's similar, citing and cited
  links, and links everything a study collects into an Obsidian knowledge
  graph of papers, MeSH concepts and searches. It is built on NCBI's
  E-utilities.
keywords:
  - PubMed
  - PubMed Central
  - literature review
  - knowledge graph
  - MeSH
  - Obsidian
  - citation network
